steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN policy returns (True, _) EXCEPT when arguments.tool_name == \"reject_discount\" AND NOT ( (arguments.verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT arguments.verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof) OR arguments.check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage OR arguments.verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings OR arguments.verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag ) ; in that case policy returns (False, \"reject_discount may be used only when a verification violation is present.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN (1) all four prerequisite result dictionaries (verify_invoice_result, check_invoice_usage_history_result, verify_contract_consistency_result, calculate_discount_rate_result) must be present; (2) verify_invoice_result.valid == True; (3) NOT (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof); (4) NOT check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage; (5) NOT (verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings OR verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag); (6) calculate_discount_rate_result.calculated_rate ∈ calculate_discount_rate_result.rate_range. IF all six conditions hold THEN policy returns (True, _) ELSE policy returns (False, appropriate reason)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"adjust_rate\" THEN (1) the same four prerequisite result dictionaries as for approve_discount must be present; (2) arguments.approval_document exists AND isinstance(arguments.approval_document, str) AND arguments.approval_document.startswith(APPROVAL_PREFIX); (3) arguments.rate is not None; (4) verify_invoice_result.valid == True; (5) NOT (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof); (6) NOT check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage; (7) NOT (verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings OR verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag); (8) arguments.rate ∈ calculate_discount_rate_result.rate_range. IF all eight conditions hold THEN policy returns (True, _) ELSE policy returns (False, appropriate reason)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ {\"approve_discount\", \"adjust_rate\"} AND (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof) THEN policy returns (False, \"Invoice >10 M without documented service‑deliverable proof.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ {\"approve_discount\", \"adjust_rate\"} AND (verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings OR verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag) THEN policy returns (False, \"Contract consistency warnings or related‑party flag present.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"reject_discount\" AND NOT ( (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof) OR check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage OR verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings OR verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag ) THEN policy returns (False, \"reject_discount may be used only when a verification violation is present.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∉ ALWAYS_ALLOWED ∪ {\"approve_discount\", \"adjust_rate\", \"reject_discount\"} THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool not subject to explicit policy restrictions.\")"
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
The statements enumerate every pre‑condition that must be satisfied before the policy can return *True* (permission) for each high‑risk tool, and they specify the exact reasons for a *False* (denial) when any condition is violated. They capture the required verification sequence, the large‑invoice proof rule, the related‑party escalation rule, the mandatory approval‑document format for rate adjustments, and the restriction that *reject_discount* is only allowed when a verification violation exists. The always‑allowed tools are permitted unconditionally, except for the special check on *reject_discount* that enforces the violation requirement. This fully translates the security request into precise, checkable logical IF‑THEN rules over the policy’s argument names and constants.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED THEN permit the call UNLESS arguments.tool_name == \"reject_discount\" AND NOT (violation_present) → DENY with reason \"reject_discount may be used only when a verification violation is present.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require (episode_id present) AND (verify_invoice_result, check_invoice_usage_history_result, verify_contract_consistency_result, calculate_discount_rate_result all exist) AND each result has source == \"tool\" AND status == \"ok\" AND episode_id matches → otherwise DENY with appropriate missing‑data message."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require verify_invoice_result.valid == true → otherwise DENY \"Invoice is not marked as valid.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require verify_invoice_result.amount ≤ MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT OR (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof == true) → otherwise DENY \"Invoice amount exceeds 10 M without service‑deliverable proof.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage == false → otherwise DENY \"Invoice over‑usage detected.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag == false AND (verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings is empty OR does not contain any high‑risk warning) → otherwise DENY \"Contract consistency warnings or related‑party flag present.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"approve_discount\" THEN require calculate_discount_rate_result.calculated_rate, min_rate, max_rate are numeric AND min_rate ≤ calculate_discount_rate_result.calculated_rate ≤ max_rate → otherwise DENY \"Calculated rate falls outside the allowed range.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"adjust_rate\" THEN the same prerequisite checks as for \"approve_discount\" must all pass (episode_id, result provenance, validity, amount limits, no over‑usage, no contract warnings) → otherwise DENY with the same reasons as above."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"adjust_rate\" THEN require arguments.approval_document is a string that matches regex ^APPROVAL_\\d{4}_\\d{3}$ → otherwise DENY \"Invalid or missing approval_document; must start with APPROVAL_ and follow format YYYY_NNN.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"adjust_rate\" THEN require arguments.rate is numeric AND min_rate ≤ arguments.rate ≤ max_rate (using the min_rate and max_rate from the latest calculate_discount_rate_result in the same episode) → otherwise DENY \"Adjusted rate is outside the allowed range.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"reject_discount\" THEN require the four prerequisite results exist, have source == \"tool\", status == \"ok\", and episode_id matches → otherwise DENY \"reject_discount prerequisite failure: …\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"reject_discount\" THEN require at least one violation among: (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof), check_invoice_usage_history_result.over_usage == true, verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag == true, or any non‑empty warnings list → otherwise DENY \"reject_discount may be used only when a verification violation is present.\""
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF (verify_invoice_result.amount > MAX_INVOICE_AMOUNT AND NOT verify_invoice_result.service_deliverable_proof) OR verify_contract_consistency_result.related_party_flag == true OR (verify_contract_consistency_result.warnings contains a string with \"high‑risk\") THEN any call to \"approve_discount\" OR \"adjust_rate\" MUST be DENIED with reason \"High‑risk condition(s) require escalation\" and the agent MUST instead call \"escalate_to_human\"."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name == \"escalate_to_human\" THEN permit the call at any time (no prerequisite checks required)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF any required field (valid, amount, over_usage, related_party_flag, warnings, calculated_rate, min_rate, max_rate) is missing from its corresponding result dict THEN DENY the high‑risk tool call with a clear error indicating the missing field."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF a result dict used in a prerequisite check does NOT contain source == \"tool\" THEN treat it as absent for the purpose of prerequisite validation and DENY the high‑risk tool call."
  }
]

The statements above encode every pre‑condition (episode consistency, successful provenance‑checked results, field presence, amount limits, usage and contract checks, rate‑range inclusion, and proper approval‑document format) and post‑condition (allow or deny) for each high‑risk tool, while explicitly permitting the always‑allowed read‑only tools and enforcing mandatory escalation on high‑risk situations. This provides a complete, machine‑checkable logical specification of the policy.

